@robinnarsinghranabhat Thank you for reporting!  I'm interested in your comment "...I expect Vllm-CC (row 1 )to be slightly better in a apples to apples comparison as it supports reasoning"

Can you help me understand this better?

Also can you help me understand the other issue you're raising?  I have run into a problem where control tokens are leaking into tool calls and have another PR that sanitizes them that's working for me in production.  If that's the issue, you can try it out [PR 35906](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/35906)

